# ── Optimizer (OpenRouter) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The optimizer route (src/app/api/optimize/route.ts) calls OpenRouter
# server-side, so the key never reaches the browser (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is required — it is the only place a key comes from, there
# is no in-app field. Without it the route returns 503 and the UI says the
# feature is not configured.
#
# OPENROUTER_MODEL is optional and overrides the default model slug
# (anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5). A model the client asks for must be in
# ALLOWED_MODELS (src/lib/optimizer/optimizer.ts); this variable is not checked
# against that list, because it is set by whoever deploys the app.
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5

# ── Rate limiting behind a reverse proxy ─────────────────────────────────────
# The route allows 20 optimizations per minute per caller, and identifies the
# caller by IP. It reads Vercel's x-vercel-forwarded-for, which the platform
# sets and clients cannot forge. Behind a different reverse proxy, set this to 1
# to fall back to x-forwarded-for — but ONLY if that proxy overwrites the header
# rather than appending to a client-supplied one, or the limit is bypassable by
# anyone who sends the header themselves.
#
# Without either header the key is the literal string "unknown", which means
# every anonymous caller shares one bucket of 20/min.
# TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1
